<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Council of Aghuen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 488</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a> · Also known as Council of Aluen</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Council of Aghuen was a church assembly convened around 488 by King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vachagan-iii">Vachagan III</a> the Pious of Caucasian Albania. Its canons, preserved in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/history-of-the-country-of-albania">History of the Country of Albania</a>, regulated the organisation and discipline of the clergy, church dues, marriage and the relations between clergy and nobility. It is a principal source for the Albanian church and society of the late fifth century.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The church, led by its own catholicos, became a central institution of the kingdom; the canons issued by King Vachagan III the Pious at the council of <b>Aghuen</b> around 488 regulated church discipline, marriage and the relations between clergy and nobility.</blockquote><a href="/empire/caucasian-albania">Caucasian Albania · Governance &amp; Law</a></li></ul></section>
